            "passage_id": "lg-game-001",
            "stem": "Which one of the following could be the order in which the associates argue, from first to fifth?",
            "choices": [
                {
                    "label": "A",
                    "text": "F, G, H, J, K"
                },
                {
                    "label": "B",
                    "text": "G, F, H, K, J"
                },
                {
                    "label": "C",
                    "text": "F, H, K, J, G"
                },
                {
                    "label": "D",
                    "text": "K, G, F, H, J"
                },
                {
                    "label": "E",
                    "text": "F, H, J, G, K"
                }
            ],
            "correct": "C",
            "explanation": "Only C satisfies all three rules. A: F=1 and H=3 are not adjacent (Rule 1). B: J is fifth, not fourth (Rule 2). D: K is first (Rule 3). E: J is third, not fourth (Rule 2). C: F-H is (1,2) ✓, J=4 ✓, K=3 ≠ 1 ✓.",
